---
title: Tool Architecture
id: tool-architecture
order: 2
description: "The architecture behind TanStack AI's tool system — server tools, client tools, call states, approval flow, and the agentic cycle."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - tool architecture
  - server tools
  - client tools
  - call states
  - approval flow
  - agentic cycle
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The TanStack AI tool system provides a powerful, flexible architecture for enabling AI agents to interact with external systems:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-tools","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Tools"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" execute securely on the backend with automatic handling"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./client-tools","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Tools"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" execute in the browser for UI updates and local operations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../chat/agentic-cycle","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Agentic Cycle"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" enables multi-step reasoning and complex workflows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#call-states","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool States"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" provide real-time feedback and enable robust UIs"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#approval-flow","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approval Flow"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" gives users control over sensitive operations\nThis architecture enables building sophisticated AI applications that can:"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fetch data from APIs and databases"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Perform calculations and transformations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update UIs and manage state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execute multi-step workflows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Require user approval for sensitive actions"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"call-flow-client-to-llm-service","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call Flow: Client to LLM Service"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a user sends a message that requires tool usage, the following flow occurs:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Browser\n    participant Server\n    participant LLM Service\n    \n    User->>Browser: Types message\n    Browser->>Server: POST /api/chat<br/>{messages, ...}\n    Server->>Server: Build tool definitions<br/>from tool array\n    Server->>LLM Service: Send request with:<br/>- messages<br/>- tool definitions<br/>- model config\n    \n    Note over LLM Service: Model analyzes tools<br/>and decides to use one\n    \n    LLM Service-->>Server: Stream chunks:<br/>tool_call, content, done\n    Server-->>Browser: Forward chunks via SSE/HTTP\n    Browser->>Browser: Parse chunks &<br/>update UI\n    Browser->>User: Show response","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-by-step-breakdown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step-by-Step Breakdown"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User Input"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The user types a message in the chat interface"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Request"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The browser sends a POST request to the server with:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current conversation history ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional data payload ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Processing"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The server:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receives the request"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extracts messages from the request body"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Converts tool definitions into the LLM's expected format"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sends the request to the LLM service (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LLM Decision"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The LLM service:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Analyzes the conversation and available tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decides whether to call a tool based on the user's request"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generates tool calls with arguments"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming Response"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The LLM streams back chunks:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool_call"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks with tool name and arguments"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks with text responses"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"done"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk when complete"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Updates"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The browser receives chunks and updates the UI in real-time"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"code-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server (API Route):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { getWeather, sendEmail } from \"./tools\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  // Create streaming chat with tools\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather, sendEmail], // Tool definitions passed here\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client (React Component):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction ChatComponent() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>{/* Render message */}</div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(e) => {\n          e.preventDefault();\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input value={input} onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)} />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={isLoading}>\n          Send\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"states-and-lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"States and Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools progress through different states during their lifecycle. Understanding these states helps build robust UIs and debug tool execution."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two parts, two state sets — this page is the canonical reference."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Call states ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaiting-input"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input-streaming"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input-complete"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-responded"},{"type":"text","value":") live on the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-call"}]},{"type":"text","value":" part as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.state"},{"type":"text","value":". There is no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"complete"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executing"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelled"},{"type":"text","value":" value on the call part. The "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"result"}]},{"type":"text","value":" lives on a separate sibling "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-result"}]},{"type":"text","value":" part whose own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streaming"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"complete"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":"; the resolved value is also mirrored onto the call part's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.output"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The diagram below is conceptual: the nodes after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-responded"},{"type":"text","value":" (executing, success, error, cancelled) are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCallState"},{"type":"text","value":" values — they correspond to the sibling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-result"},{"type":"text","value":" part's state ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"complete"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":") and the call part's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"output"},{"type":"text","value":" field."}]},{"type":"code","value":"stateDiagram-v2\n    state \"tool-call part (ToolCallState)\" as Call {\n        [*] --> AwaitingInput: tool_call received\n        AwaitingInput --> InputStreaming: partial arguments\n        InputStreaming --> InputComplete: all arguments received\n        InputComplete --> ApprovalRequested: needsApproval=true\n        ApprovalRequested --> ApprovalResponded: user approves / denies\n    }\n    InputComplete --> ResultComplete: needsApproval=false, success\n    InputComplete --> ResultError: parsing, validation, or execution error\n    ApprovalResponded --> ResultComplete: approved + success (output set)\n    ApprovalResponded --> ResultError: approved + error\n    ApprovalResponded --> Denied: user denied (no execution)\n    state \"tool-result part\" as Results {\n        ResultComplete: complete\n        ResultError: error\n    }\n    ResultComplete --> [*]\n    ResultError --> [*]\n    Denied --> [*]","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"call-states","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call States"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Action"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaiting-input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool call received, no arguments yet"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show loading"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input-streaming"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Partial arguments being received"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show progress"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input-complete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All arguments received"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ready to execute"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Waiting for user approval"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show approval UI"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-responded"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User has approved/denied"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execute or cancel"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"result-states","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result States"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Action"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streaming"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result being streamed (future feature)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show progress"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"complete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result is complete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show result"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error occurred before or during execution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show error message"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"monitoring-tool-states-in-react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitoring Tool States in React"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { createChatClientOptions } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { getWeather, sendEmail } from \"./tools\";\nimport { ApprovalUI } from \"./approval-ui\";\n\n// Wiring `tools` is what lets `part.name` / `part.input` / `part.output`\n// narrow to each tool's types below.\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools: [getWeather, sendEmail],\n});\n\nfunction ChatComponent() {\n  const { messages } = useChat(chatOptions);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part) => {\n            if (part.type === \"tool-call\") {\n              return (\n                <div key={part.id} className=\"tool-status\">\n                  {/* Show state-specific UI */}\n                  {part.state === \"awaiting-input\" && (\n                    <div>🔄 Calling {part.name}...</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"input-streaming\" && (\n                    <div>📥 Receiving arguments...</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"input-complete\" && (\n                    <div>✓ Arguments ready</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"approval-requested\" && (\n                    <ApprovalUI part={part} />\n                  )}\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"tool-result\") {\n              return (\n                <div key={part.toolCallId}>\n                  {part.state === \"complete\" && (\n                    <div>✓ Tool completed</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"error\" && (\n                    <div>❌ Error: {part.error}</div>\n                  )}\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"approval-flow","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approval Flow"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For sensitive operations, tools can require user approval before execution:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n    participant LLM\n    participant Tool\n    \n    LLM->>Server: tool_call: send_email\n    Server->>Server: Check needsApproval\n    Server->>Client: approval-requested chunk\n    Client->>Client: Show approval UI\n    User->>Client: Clicks \"Approve\"\n    Client->>Server: POST approval response\n    Server->>Tool: execute(args)\n    Tool-->>Server: result\n    Server->>LLM: tool_result\n    LLM-->>Client: Generate response","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define tool with approval:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { emailService } from \"./email-service\";\n\nconst sendEmailDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"send_email\",\n  description: \"Send an email\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    to: z.string().email(),\n    subject: z.string(),\n    body: z.string(),\n  }),\n  needsApproval: true, // Requires user approval\n});\n\nconst sendEmail = sendEmailDef.server(async ({ to, subject, body }) => {\n  await emailService.send({ to, subject, body });\n  return { success: true };\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle approval in client:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { messages, addToolApprovalResponse } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n\n// In your render (guard `type` and `approval` so `part.approval.id` is safe):\n{part.type === \"tool-call\" &&\n  part.state === \"approval-requested\" &&\n  part.approval && (\n    <div>\n      <p>Approve sending email to {part.input.to}?</p>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          addToolApprovalResponse({\n            id: part.approval.id,\n            approved: true,\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Approve\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          addToolApprovalResponse({\n            id: part.approval.id,\n            approved: false,\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Deny\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hybrid-tools-server-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hybrid Tools (Server + Client)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some tools need to execute in both environments:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\nimport { i18n } from \"./i18n\";\n\n// Server: Fetch data from database\nconst fetchUserPrefsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"fetch_user_preferences\",\n  description: \"Get user preferences from server\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    userId: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst fetchUserPreferences = fetchUserPrefsDef.server(async ({ userId }) => {\n  const prefs = await db.userPreferences.findUnique({ where: { userId } });\n  return prefs;\n});\n\n// Client: Apply preferences to UI\nconst applyPrefsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"apply_preferences\",\n  description: \"Apply user preferences to the UI\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    theme: z.string(),\n    language: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\n// On client, create client implementation\nconst applyPreferences = applyPrefsDef.client(async ({ theme, language }) => {\n  // Update UI state with preferences\n  document.body.className = theme;\n  i18n.changeLanguage(language);\n  return { applied: true };\n});\n\n// Usage: LLM can chain these together\n// 1. Call fetchUserPreferences (server)\n// 2. Call applyPreferences with the result (client)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parallel-tool-execution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parallel Tool Execution"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM can call multiple tools in parallel for efficiency:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"graph TD\n    A[LLM decides to call 3 tools] --> B[tool_call index: 0]\n    A --> C[tool_call index: 1]\n    A --> D[tool_call index: 2]\n    B --> E[Execute in parallel]\n    C --> E\n    D --> E\n    E --> F[Collect all results]\n    F --> G[Continue with results]","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"User: \"Compare the weather in NYC, SF, and LA\"\n\nLLM calls:\n- get_weather({city: \"NYC\"}) [index: 0]\n- get_weather({city: \"SF\"}) [index: 1]\n- get_weather({city: \"LA\"}) [index: 2]\n\nAll execute simultaneously, then LLM generates comparison."},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server tools of one model turn start together, and the model gets their results in the order of its calls. To run them one at a time, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./tools#run-tools-one-at-a-time","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run tools one at a time"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best Practices"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tool-design","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool Design"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Single Responsibility"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Each tool should do one thing well"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear Descriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Help the LLM understand when to use the tool"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use Zod schemas for input/output validation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Return meaningful error messages, don't throw"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Idempotency"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Tools should be safe to call multiple times"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"security","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server vs Client"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Put sensitive operations on the server"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approval Flow"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval"},{"type":"text","value":" for destructive actions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input Validation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Always validate tool inputs"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate Limiting"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Implement rate limits for expensive tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audit Logs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Log tool executions for debugging and security"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"performance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caching"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Cache tool results when appropriate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parallel Execution"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Enable parallel tool calls when possible"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use streaming for long-running operations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Timeouts"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Set timeouts for external API calls"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lazy Loading"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Load tools only when needed"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Basic tool concepts and examples"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Deep dive into server-side tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./client-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Deep dive into client-side tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool Approval Flow"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Implementing approval workflows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI protocol"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Understanding the streaming protocol"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"call-flow-client-to-llm-service","text":"Call Flow: Client to LLM Service","level":2},{"id":"step-by-step-breakdown","text":"Step-by-Step Breakdown","level":3},{"id":"code-example","text":"Code Example","level":3},{"id":"states-and-lifecycle","text":"States and Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"call-states","text":"Call States","level":3},{"id":"result-states","text":"Result States","level":3},{"id":"monitoring-tool-states-in-react","text":"Monitoring Tool States in React","level":3},{"id":"approval-flow","text":"Approval Flow","level":3},{"id":"hybrid-tools-server-client","text":"Hybrid Tools (Server + Client)","level":3},{"id":"parallel-tool-execution","text":"Parallel Tool Execution","level":3},{"id":"best-practices","text":"Best Practices","level":2},{"id":"tool-design","text":"Tool Design","level":3},{"id":"security","text":"Security","level":3},{"id":"performance","text":"Performance","level":3},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe TanStack AI tool system provides a powerful, flexible architecture for enabling AI agents to interact with external systems:\n\n- [**Server Tools**](./server-tools) execute securely on the backend with automatic handling\n- [**Client Tools**](./client-tools) execute in the browser for UI updates and local operations\n- [**The Agentic Cycle**](../chat/agentic-cycle) enables multi-step reasoning and complex workflows\n- [**Tool States**](#call-states) provide real-time feedback and enable robust UIs\n- [**Approval Flow**](#approval-flow) gives users control over sensitive operations\nThis architecture enables building sophisticated AI applications that can:\n\n- Fetch data from APIs and databases\n- Perform calculations and transformations\n- Update UIs and manage state\n- Execute multi-step workflows\n- Require user approval for sensitive actions\n\n## Call Flow: Client to LLM Service\n\nWhen a user sends a message that requires tool usage, the following flow occurs:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Browser\n    participant Server\n    participant LLM Service\n    \n    User->>Browser: Types message\n    Browser->>Server: POST /api/chat<br/>{messages, ...}\n    Server->>Server: Build tool definitions<br/>from tool array\n    Server->>LLM Service: Send request with:<br/>- messages<br/>- tool definitions<br/>- model config\n    \n    Note over LLM Service: Model analyzes tools<br/>and decides to use one\n    \n    LLM Service-->>Server: Stream chunks:<br/>tool_call, content, done\n    Server-->>Browser: Forward chunks via SSE/HTTP\n    Browser->>Browser: Parse chunks &<br/>update UI\n    Browser->>User: Show response\n```\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown\n\n1. **User Input**: The user types a message in the chat interface\n2. **Client Request**: The browser sends a POST request to the server with:\n   - Current conversation history (`messages`)\n   - Optional data payload (`body`)\n3. **Server Processing**: The server:\n   - Receives the request\n   - Extracts messages from the request body\n   - Converts tool definitions into the LLM's expected format\n   - Sends the request to the LLM service (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)\n4. **LLM Decision**: The LLM service:\n   - Analyzes the conversation and available tools\n   - Decides whether to call a tool based on the user's request\n   - Generates tool calls with arguments\n5. **Streaming Response**: The LLM streams back chunks:\n   - `tool_call` chunks with tool name and arguments\n   - `content` chunks with text responses\n   - `done` chunk when complete\n6. **Client Updates**: The browser receives chunks and updates the UI in real-time\n\n### Code Example\n\n**Server (API Route):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { getWeather, sendEmail } from \"./tools\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  // Create streaming chat with tools\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather, sendEmail], // Tool definitions passed here\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n**Client (React Component):**\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction ChatComponent() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>{/* Render message */}</div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(e) => {\n          e.preventDefault();\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input value={input} onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)} />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={isLoading}>\n          Send\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## States and Lifecycle\n\nTools progress through different states during their lifecycle. Understanding these states helps build robust UIs and debug tool execution.\n\n> **Two parts, two state sets — this page is the canonical reference.** Call states (`awaiting-input`, `input-streaming`, `input-complete`, `approval-requested`, `approval-responded`) live on the **`tool-call`** part as `part.state`. There is no `complete`/`error`/`executing`/`cancelled` value on the call part. The *result* lives on a separate sibling **`tool-result`** part whose own `state` is `streaming`, `complete`, or `error`; the resolved value is also mirrored onto the call part's `part.output`.\n\nThe diagram below is conceptual: the nodes after `approval-responded` (executing, success, error, cancelled) are **not** `ToolCallState` values — they correspond to the sibling `tool-result` part's state (`complete` / `error`) and the call part's `output` field.\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    state \"tool-call part (ToolCallState)\" as Call {\n        [*] --> AwaitingInput: tool_call received\n        AwaitingInput --> InputStreaming: partial arguments\n        InputStreaming --> InputComplete: all arguments received\n        InputComplete --> ApprovalRequested: needsApproval=true\n        ApprovalRequested --> ApprovalResponded: user approves / denies\n    }\n    InputComplete --> ResultComplete: needsApproval=false, success\n    InputComplete --> ResultError: parsing, validation, or execution error\n    ApprovalResponded --> ResultComplete: approved + success (output set)\n    ApprovalResponded --> ResultError: approved + error\n    ApprovalResponded --> Denied: user denied (no execution)\n    state \"tool-result part\" as Results {\n        ResultComplete: complete\n        ResultError: error\n    }\n    ResultComplete --> [*]\n    ResultError --> [*]\n    Denied --> [*]\n```\n\n### Call States\n\n| State | Description | Client Action |\n|-------|-------------|---------------|\n| `awaiting-input` | Tool call received, no arguments yet | Show loading |\n| `input-streaming` | Partial arguments being received | Show progress |\n| `input-complete` | All arguments received | Ready to execute |\n| `approval-requested` | Waiting for user approval | Show approval UI |\n| `approval-responded` | User has approved/denied | Execute or cancel |\n\n### Result States\n\n| State | Description | Client Action |\n|-------|-------------|---------------|\n| `streaming` | Result being streamed (future feature) | Show progress |\n| `complete` | Result is complete | Show result |\n| `error` | Error occurred before or during execution | Show error message |\n\n### Monitoring Tool States in React\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { createChatClientOptions } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { getWeather, sendEmail } from \"./tools\";\nimport { ApprovalUI } from \"./approval-ui\";\n\n// Wiring `tools` is what lets `part.name` / `part.input` / `part.output`\n// narrow to each tool's types below.\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools: [getWeather, sendEmail],\n});\n\nfunction ChatComponent() {\n  const { messages } = useChat(chatOptions);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part) => {\n            if (part.type === \"tool-call\") {\n              return (\n                <div key={part.id} className=\"tool-status\">\n                  {/* Show state-specific UI */}\n                  {part.state === \"awaiting-input\" && (\n                    <div>🔄 Calling {part.name}...</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"input-streaming\" && (\n                    <div>📥 Receiving arguments...</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"input-complete\" && (\n                    <div>✓ Arguments ready</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"approval-requested\" && (\n                    <ApprovalUI part={part} />\n                  )}\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"tool-result\") {\n              return (\n                <div key={part.toolCallId}>\n                  {part.state === \"complete\" && (\n                    <div>✓ Tool completed</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"error\" && (\n                    <div>❌ Error: {part.error}</div>\n                  )}\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Approval Flow\n\nFor sensitive operations, tools can require user approval before execution:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n    participant LLM\n    participant Tool\n    \n    LLM->>Server: tool_call: send_email\n    Server->>Server: Check needsApproval\n    Server->>Client: approval-requested chunk\n    Client->>Client: Show approval UI\n    User->>Client: Clicks \"Approve\"\n    Client->>Server: POST approval response\n    Server->>Tool: execute(args)\n    Tool-->>Server: result\n    Server->>LLM: tool_result\n    LLM-->>Client: Generate response\n```\n\n**Define tool with approval:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { emailService } from \"./email-service\";\n\nconst sendEmailDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"send_email\",\n  description: \"Send an email\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    to: z.string().email(),\n    subject: z.string(),\n    body: z.string(),\n  }),\n  needsApproval: true, // Requires user approval\n});\n\nconst sendEmail = sendEmailDef.server(async ({ to, subject, body }) => {\n  await emailService.send({ to, subject, body });\n  return { success: true };\n});\n```\n\n**Handle approval in client:**\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst { messages, addToolApprovalResponse } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n\n// In your render (guard `type` and `approval` so `part.approval.id` is safe):\n{part.type === \"tool-call\" &&\n  part.state === \"approval-requested\" &&\n  part.approval && (\n    <div>\n      <p>Approve sending email to {part.input.to}?</p>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          addToolApprovalResponse({\n            id: part.approval.id,\n            approved: true,\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Approve\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          addToolApprovalResponse({\n            id: part.approval.id,\n            approved: false,\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Deny\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )}\n```\n\n### Hybrid Tools (Server + Client)\n\nSome tools need to execute in both environments:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\nimport { i18n } from \"./i18n\";\n\n// Server: Fetch data from database\nconst fetchUserPrefsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"fetch_user_preferences\",\n  description: \"Get user preferences from server\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    userId: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst fetchUserPreferences = fetchUserPrefsDef.server(async ({ userId }) => {\n  const prefs = await db.userPreferences.findUnique({ where: { userId } });\n  return prefs;\n});\n\n// Client: Apply preferences to UI\nconst applyPrefsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"apply_preferences\",\n  description: \"Apply user preferences to the UI\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    theme: z.string(),\n    language: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\n// On client, create client implementation\nconst applyPreferences = applyPrefsDef.client(async ({ theme, language }) => {\n  // Update UI state with preferences\n  document.body.className = theme;\n  i18n.changeLanguage(language);\n  return { applied: true };\n});\n\n// Usage: LLM can chain these together\n// 1. Call fetchUserPreferences (server)\n// 2. Call applyPreferences with the result (client)\n```\n\n### Parallel Tool Execution\n\nThe LLM can call multiple tools in parallel for efficiency:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[LLM decides to call 3 tools] --> B[tool_call index: 0]\n    A --> C[tool_call index: 1]\n    A --> D[tool_call index: 2]\n    B --> E[Execute in parallel]\n    C --> E\n    D --> E\n    E --> F[Collect all results]\n    F --> G[Continue with results]\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\nUser: \"Compare the weather in NYC, SF, and LA\"\n\nLLM calls:\n- get_weather({city: \"NYC\"}) [index: 0]\n- get_weather({city: \"SF\"}) [index: 1]\n- get_weather({city: \"LA\"}) [index: 2]\n\nAll execute simultaneously, then LLM generates comparison.\n```\n\nThe server tools of one model turn start together, and the model gets their results in the order of its calls. To run them one at a time, see [Run tools one at a time](./tools#run-tools-one-at-a-time).\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Tool Design\n\n- **Single Responsibility**: Each tool should do one thing well\n- **Clear Descriptions**: Help the LLM understand when to use the tool\n- **Type Safety**: Use Zod schemas for input/output validation\n- **Error Handling**: Return meaningful error messages, don't throw\n- **Idempotency**: Tools should be safe to call multiple times\n\n### Security\n\n- **Server vs Client**: Put sensitive operations on the server\n- **Approval Flow**: Use `needsApproval` for destructive actions\n- **Input Validation**: Always validate tool inputs\n- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limits for expensive tools\n- **Audit Logs**: Log tool executions for debugging and security\n\n### Performance\n\n- **Caching**: Cache tool results when appropriate\n- **Parallel Execution**: Enable parallel tool calls when possible\n- **Streaming**: Use streaming for long-running operations\n- **Timeouts**: Set timeouts for external API calls\n- **Lazy Loading**: Load tools only when needed\n\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Tools Overview](./tools) - Basic tool concepts and examples\n- [Server Tools](./server-tools) - Deep dive into server-side tools\n- [Client Tools](./client-tools) - Deep dive into client-side tools\n- [Tool Approval Flow](./tool-approval) - Implementing approval workflows\n- [AG-UI protocol](https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction) - Understanding the streaming protocol\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Tool Architecture\nid: tool-architecture\norder: 2\ndescription: \"The architecture behind TanStack AI's tool system — server tools, client tools, call states, approval flow, and the agentic cycle.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - tool architecture\n  - server tools\n  - client tools\n  - call states\n  - approval flow\n  - agentic cycle\n---\n\nThe TanStack AI tool system provides a powerful, flexible architecture for enabling AI agents to interact with external systems:\n\n- [**Server Tools**](./server-tools) execute securely on the backend with automatic handling\n- [**Client Tools**](./client-tools) execute in the browser for UI updates and local operations\n- [**The Agentic Cycle**](../chat/agentic-cycle) enables multi-step reasoning and complex workflows\n- [**Tool States**](#call-states) provide real-time feedback and enable robust UIs\n- [**Approval Flow**](#approval-flow) gives users control over sensitive operations\nThis architecture enables building sophisticated AI applications that can:\n\n- Fetch data from APIs and databases\n- Perform calculations and transformations\n- Update UIs and manage state\n- Execute multi-step workflows\n- Require user approval for sensitive actions\n\n## Call Flow: Client to LLM Service\n\nWhen a user sends a message that requires tool usage, the following flow occurs:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Browser\n    participant Server\n    participant LLM Service\n    \n    User->>Browser: Types message\n    Browser->>Server: POST /api/chat<br/>{messages, ...}\n    Server->>Server: Build tool definitions<br/>from tool array\n    Server->>LLM Service: Send request with:<br/>- messages<br/>- tool definitions<br/>- model config\n    \n    Note over LLM Service: Model analyzes tools<br/>and decides to use one\n    \n    LLM Service-->>Server: Stream chunks:<br/>tool_call, content, done\n    Server-->>Browser: Forward chunks via SSE/HTTP\n    Browser->>Browser: Parse chunks &<br/>update UI\n    Browser->>User: Show response\n```\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown\n\n1. **User Input**: The user types a message in the chat interface\n2. **Client Request**: The browser sends a POST request to the server with:\n   - Current conversation history (`messages`)\n   - Optional data payload (`body`)\n3. **Server Processing**: The server:\n   - Receives the request\n   - Extracts messages from the request body\n   - Converts tool definitions into the LLM's expected format\n   - Sends the request to the LLM service (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)\n4. **LLM Decision**: The LLM service:\n   - Analyzes the conversation and available tools\n   - Decides whether to call a tool based on the user's request\n   - Generates tool calls with arguments\n5. **Streaming Response**: The LLM streams back chunks:\n   - `tool_call` chunks with tool name and arguments\n   - `content` chunks with text responses\n   - `done` chunk when complete\n6. **Client Updates**: The browser receives chunks and updates the UI in real-time\n\n### Code Example\n\n**Server (API Route):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { getWeather, sendEmail } from \"./tools\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  // Create streaming chat with tools\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather, sendEmail], // Tool definitions passed here\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n**Client (React Component):**\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction ChatComponent() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>{/* Render message */}</div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(e) => {\n          e.preventDefault();\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input value={input} onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)} />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={isLoading}>\n          Send\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## States and Lifecycle\n\nTools progress through different states during their lifecycle. Understanding these states helps build robust UIs and debug tool execution.\n\n> **Two parts, two state sets — this page is the canonical reference.** Call states (`awaiting-input`, `input-streaming`, `input-complete`, `approval-requested`, `approval-responded`) live on the **`tool-call`** part as `part.state`. There is no `complete`/`error`/`executing`/`cancelled` value on the call part. The *result* lives on a separate sibling **`tool-result`** part whose own `state` is `streaming`, `complete`, or `error`; the resolved value is also mirrored onto the call part's `part.output`.\n\nThe diagram below is conceptual: the nodes after `approval-responded` (executing, success, error, cancelled) are **not** `ToolCallState` values — they correspond to the sibling `tool-result` part's state (`complete` / `error`) and the call part's `output` field.\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    state \"tool-call part (ToolCallState)\" as Call {\n        [*] --> AwaitingInput: tool_call received\n        AwaitingInput --> InputStreaming: partial arguments\n        InputStreaming --> InputComplete: all arguments received\n        InputComplete --> ApprovalRequested: needsApproval=true\n        ApprovalRequested --> ApprovalResponded: user approves / denies\n    }\n    InputComplete --> ResultComplete: needsApproval=false, success\n    InputComplete --> ResultError: parsing, validation, or execution error\n    ApprovalResponded --> ResultComplete: approved + success (output set)\n    ApprovalResponded --> ResultError: approved + error\n    ApprovalResponded --> Denied: user denied (no execution)\n    state \"tool-result part\" as Results {\n        ResultComplete: complete\n        ResultError: error\n    }\n    ResultComplete --> [*]\n    ResultError --> [*]\n    Denied --> [*]\n```\n\n### Call States\n\n| State | Description | Client Action |\n|-------|-------------|---------------|\n| `awaiting-input` | Tool call received, no arguments yet | Show loading |\n| `input-streaming` | Partial arguments being received | Show progress |\n| `input-complete` | All arguments received | Ready to execute |\n| `approval-requested` | Waiting for user approval | Show approval UI |\n| `approval-responded` | User has approved/denied | Execute or cancel |\n\n### Result States\n\n| State | Description | Client Action |\n|-------|-------------|---------------|\n| `streaming` | Result being streamed (future feature) | Show progress |\n| `complete` | Result is complete | Show result |\n| `error` | Error occurred before or during execution | Show error message |\n\n### Monitoring Tool States in React\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { createChatClientOptions } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { getWeather, sendEmail } from \"./tools\";\nimport { ApprovalUI } from \"./approval-ui\";\n\n// Wiring `tools` is what lets `part.name` / `part.input` / `part.output`\n// narrow to each tool's types below.\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools: [getWeather, sendEmail],\n});\n\nfunction ChatComponent() {\n  const { messages } = useChat(chatOptions);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part) => {\n            if (part.type === \"tool-call\") {\n              return (\n                <div key={part.id} className=\"tool-status\">\n                  {/* Show state-specific UI */}\n                  {part.state === \"awaiting-input\" && (\n                    <div>🔄 Calling {part.name}...</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"input-streaming\" && (\n                    <div>📥 Receiving arguments...</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"input-complete\" && (\n                    <div>✓ Arguments ready</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"approval-requested\" && (\n                    <ApprovalUI part={part} />\n                  )}\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"tool-result\") {\n              return (\n                <div key={part.toolCallId}>\n                  {part.state === \"complete\" && (\n                    <div>✓ Tool completed</div>\n                  )}\n                  {part.state === \"error\" && (\n                    <div>❌ Error: {part.error}</div>\n                  )}\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Approval Flow\n\nFor sensitive operations, tools can require user approval before execution:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n    participant LLM\n    participant Tool\n    \n    LLM->>Server: tool_call: send_email\n    Server->>Server: Check needsApproval\n    Server->>Client: approval-requested chunk\n    Client->>Client: Show approval UI\n    User->>Client: Clicks \"Approve\"\n    Client->>Server: POST approval response\n    Server->>Tool: execute(args)\n    Tool-->>Server: result\n    Server->>LLM: tool_result\n    LLM-->>Client: Generate response\n```\n\n**Define tool with approval:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { emailService } from \"./email-service\";\n\nconst sendEmailDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"send_email\",\n  description: \"Send an email\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    to: z.string().email(),\n    subject: z.string(),\n    body: z.string(),\n  }),\n  needsApproval: true, // Requires user approval\n});\n\nconst sendEmail = sendEmailDef.server(async ({ to, subject, body }) => {\n  await emailService.send({ to, subject, body });\n  return { success: true };\n});\n```\n\n**Handle approval in client:**\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst { messages, addToolApprovalResponse } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n\n// In your render (guard `type` and `approval` so `part.approval.id` is safe):\n{part.type === \"tool-call\" &&\n  part.state === \"approval-requested\" &&\n  part.approval && (\n    <div>\n      <p>Approve sending email to {part.input.to}?</p>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          addToolApprovalResponse({\n            id: part.approval.id,\n            approved: true,\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Approve\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          addToolApprovalResponse({\n            id: part.approval.id,\n            approved: false,\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Deny\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )}\n```\n\n### Hybrid Tools (Server + Client)\n\nSome tools need to execute in both environments:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\nimport { i18n } from \"./i18n\";\n\n// Server: Fetch data from database\nconst fetchUserPrefsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"fetch_user_preferences\",\n  description: \"Get user preferences from server\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    userId: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst fetchUserPreferences = fetchUserPrefsDef.server(async ({ userId }) => {\n  const prefs = await db.userPreferences.findUnique({ where: { userId } });\n  return prefs;\n});\n\n// Client: Apply preferences to UI\nconst applyPrefsDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"apply_preferences\",\n  description: \"Apply user preferences to the UI\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    theme: z.string(),\n    language: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\n// On client, create client implementation\nconst applyPreferences = applyPrefsDef.client(async ({ theme, language }) => {\n  // Update UI state with preferences\n  document.body.className = theme;\n  i18n.changeLanguage(language);\n  return { applied: true };\n});\n\n// Usage: LLM can chain these together\n// 1. Call fetchUserPreferences (server)\n// 2. Call applyPreferences with the result (client)\n```\n\n### Parallel Tool Execution\n\nThe LLM can call multiple tools in parallel for efficiency:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[LLM decides to call 3 tools] --> B[tool_call index: 0]\n    A --> C[tool_call index: 1]\n    A --> D[tool_call index: 2]\n    B --> E[Execute in parallel]\n    C --> E\n    D --> E\n    E --> F[Collect all results]\n    F --> G[Continue with results]\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\nUser: \"Compare the weather in NYC, SF, and LA\"\n\nLLM calls:\n- get_weather({city: \"NYC\"}) [index: 0]\n- get_weather({city: \"SF\"}) [index: 1]\n- get_weather({city: \"LA\"}) [index: 2]\n\nAll execute simultaneously, then LLM generates comparison.\n```\n\nThe server tools of one model turn start together, and the model gets their results in the order of its calls. To run them one at a time, see [Run tools one at a time](./tools#run-tools-one-at-a-time).\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Tool Design\n\n- **Single Responsibility**: Each tool should do one thing well\n- **Clear Descriptions**: Help the LLM understand when to use the tool\n- **Type Safety**: Use Zod schemas for input/output validation\n- **Error Handling**: Return meaningful error messages, don't throw\n- **Idempotency**: Tools should be safe to call multiple times\n\n### Security\n\n- **Server vs Client**: Put sensitive operations on the server\n- **Approval Flow**: Use `needsApproval` for destructive actions\n- **Input Validation**: Always validate tool inputs\n- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limits for expensive tools\n- **Audit Logs**: Log tool executions for debugging and security\n\n### Performance\n\n- **Caching**: Cache tool results when appropriate\n- **Parallel Execution**: Enable parallel tool calls when possible\n- **Streaming**: Use streaming for long-running operations\n- **Timeouts**: Set timeouts for external API calls\n- **Lazy Loading**: Load tools only when needed\n\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Tools Overview](./tools) - Basic tool concepts and examples\n- [Server Tools](./server-tools) - Deep dive into server-side tools\n- [Client Tools](./client-tools) - Deep dive into client-side tools\n- [Tool Approval Flow](./tool-approval) - Implementing approval workflows\n- [AG-UI protocol](https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction) - Understanding the streaming protocol\n"}
